 "brief": "A cantilever latch hook in PA12 (SLS) that holds a lid shut. Its foot is a pad on the plane z = 0 (x = -8 to 8, y = -6 to 6) held by two M3 screws that go down through the pad into the housing at y = 0, x = -4.5 and 4.5. The arm stands up along Z to a catch at z = 32 to 36 that hooks over the lid's edge toward +y (the catch reaches to y = 5). Keep it inside x = -8 to 8, y = -6 to 6, z = 0 to 36. The lid pulls up on the underside of the catch with 60 N; to release, a thumb pushes the top of the arm toward -y with 8 N. Safety factor 2.",
